WEBVTT

00:08.110 --> 00:10.190
Today's our first day as sophomores!

00:10.190 --> 00:12.170
I'm glad I wasn't held back.

00:12.170 --> 00:13.820
It's thanks to you and Seika.

00:13.820 --> 00:17.530
No, it's because you worked really hard!

00:17.770 --> 00:20.530
My grades weren't looking so 
good, so it was a big help.

00:21.200 --> 00:23.280
This food's great, too.

00:23.280 --> 00:26.320
I didn't have time to eat it 
last year, so I had no idea.

00:26.320 --> 00:28.490
There was that demon attack, after all.

00:28.490 --> 00:29.340
Yup.

00:29.340 --> 00:31.960
Amyu, this duck meat is great.

00:31.960 --> 00:35.740
<i>Surprisingly, there've been no 
more demon attacks since then.</i>

00:35.740 --> 00:37.930
<i>It's a bit of a letdown.</i>

00:37.930 --> 00:40.430
<i>I've got wards up all around the school,</i>

00:40.720 --> 00:42.930
<i>but there aren't any signs of assassins.</i>

00:42.930 --> 00:46.060
<i>This year's entrance ceremony 
should end without incident.</i>

00:48.410 --> 00:50.400
Seika Lamprogue.

00:50.780 --> 00:52.610
Vice-principal?

00:52.610 --> 00:57.960
You and Yifa are to come to the 
principal's office tomorrow evening.

00:57.960 --> 00:59.700
Farewell.

01:00.880 --> 01:03.580
Looks like somebody's in trouble!

01:03.580 --> 01:05.180
Think they're gonna expel you?

01:05.180 --> 01:07.230
Don't say that.

01:07.230 --> 01:08.630
Yifa was summoned, too.

01:09.110 --> 01:13.130
<i>Jokes aside, I've got a 
bad feeling about this.</i>

01:36.240 --> 01:47.330
<b>The Reincarnation of
the Strongest Exorcist in Another World</b>

02:49.770 --> 02:53.550
I've never met the Principal.

02:53.550 --> 02:54.490
Me, neither.

02:54.490 --> 02:59.160
It's always been the vice-principal 
whenever there was an event, right?

02:59.160 --> 02:59.780
Yeah.

03:00.350 --> 03:03.900
I thought it was some big shot from the 
capital who just put their name down.

03:03.900 --> 03:05.290
I guess they're real, though.

03:09.600 --> 03:10.570
Come in.

03:11.630 --> 03:12.920
Excuse us.

03:12.920 --> 03:14.420
Excuse us.

03:17.400 --> 03:20.300
Welcome, Lamprogue boy.

03:23.150 --> 03:24.990
I'm a little surprised.

03:24.990 --> 03:28.680
I was expecting a little brat who 
was far too proud of himself.

03:29.140 --> 03:32.220
But instead I see someone who 
looks like he's seen some things.

03:33.050 --> 03:34.360
Thank you.

03:34.360 --> 03:36.200
I, too, am surprised

03:36.200 --> 03:39.860
to find that a demihuman is the leader 
of the Imperial Magic Academy.

03:40.110 --> 03:42.950
I dislike that term.

03:42.950 --> 03:45.940
We're not beneath humans in any way.

03:45.940 --> 03:49.040
Even calling us "demons" would be better.

03:49.330 --> 03:52.630
<i>True. If you want to be strict 
about it, dwarves are demons, too.</i>

03:52.630 --> 03:54.220
My apologies.

03:55.200 --> 03:59.740
Hmph. I guess if you're 
acting that way around me,

03:59.740 --> 04:03.060
it means that whatever you've seen 
has given you a lot of confidence.

04:03.770 --> 04:06.140
I can tell you're related to him, at least.

04:06.520 --> 04:08.310
You know my father?

04:08.570 --> 04:11.480
No, I mean your uncle.

04:11.480 --> 04:16.020
<i>I never heard anything about 
my father having siblings.</i>

04:16.610 --> 04:19.180
Well, that doesn't matter.

04:19.180 --> 04:21.070
Let's get to the point.

04:21.640 --> 04:22.700
That being?

04:23.340 --> 04:27.870
I want you to enter a mixed disciplines combat 
tournament being held in the capital.

04:28.150 --> 04:29.900
With her.

04:32.180 --> 04:33.710
Thank you for coming.

04:34.080 --> 04:37.040
Now, tell your upperclassmen your name.

04:38.090 --> 04:39.670
Mabel Crane.

04:40.050 --> 04:43.090
Episode 5       Mabel Crane

04:43.360 --> 04:44.900
A new student?

04:44.900 --> 04:47.680
The academy's been given
two slots at the tournament.

04:47.680 --> 04:49.510
Mabel's one.

04:49.890 --> 04:55.140
Will the other be you, or your servant girl?

04:58.980 --> 05:01.860
Why didn't I get invited?

05:01.860 --> 05:03.780
I said the same thing.

05:03.780 --> 05:06.200
So you're going?

05:09.310 --> 05:12.480
Yeah. There's something I'm curious about.

05:13.620 --> 05:18.730
Did the Magic Academy ever participate 
in this tournament before?

05:18.730 --> 05:23.800
The rules changed this year, 
and now magic's allowed.

05:23.800 --> 05:27.350
And the academy was given slots.

05:27.350 --> 05:29.770
From the sound of it,

05:29.770 --> 05:34.180
she wanted us to go to boost 
the academy's reputation.

05:34.400 --> 05:38.480
Isn't that usually a job 
for the upperclassmen?

05:38.790 --> 05:44.010
Supposedly they're all too 
busy with their own research.

05:45.440 --> 05:47.490
Why you, though?

05:47.830 --> 05:50.760
He came back alive from the 
dungeon last year, right?

05:50.760 --> 05:57.290
And the principal knew he defeated 
an elder newt before coming here.

05:57.740 --> 06:01.840
That only makes it weirder that it wasn't me!

06:01.840 --> 06:03.210
She mentioned that.

06:03.860 --> 06:08.740
I've decided the two of you are better. 
That's all there is to it.

06:08.740 --> 06:12.760
Don't underestimate the
gut instincts of your elders.

06:13.270 --> 06:14.350
She said.

06:14.350 --> 06:15.610
Why?

06:15.610 --> 06:19.350
I don't know about magic, but I'm 
better with a sword than anyone!

06:20.850 --> 06:23.200
I knew you'd say that.

06:23.200 --> 06:24.650
Did you want to go, then?

06:24.880 --> 06:26.160
Well...

06:27.730 --> 06:30.820
Actually, now that I think about it, I don't.

06:32.670 --> 06:36.100
They said if you win, 
you get a ton of prize money

06:36.100 --> 06:38.580
and a chance to join the Royal Guards.

06:38.580 --> 06:43.680
Well, I'd like the money, but I'm 
not interested in joining the guard.

06:43.680 --> 06:47.970
And fighting people isn't nearly 
as much fun as fighting monsters.

06:47.970 --> 06:51.300
<i>That's strange. 
I thought Amyu just loved to fight.</i>

06:51.800 --> 06:54.970
<i>Maybe she's mellowed a bit.</i>

06:55.280 --> 06:59.100
I still don't like the 
fact they didn't ask me.

06:59.400 --> 07:02.640
Maybe they didn't want to send out
somebody who was too strong?

07:02.640 --> 07:06.780
It could mean losing them to the Royal Guard.

07:06.780 --> 07:09.360
Then, why choose you?

07:09.360 --> 07:13.240
Me? I'm not that strong.

07:14.610 --> 07:17.660
Cut it out with that
fake smile of yours.

07:17.940 --> 07:20.260
I don't get it, though.

07:20.260 --> 07:23.890
You, I understand, but why Yifa?

07:25.930 --> 07:27.380
That's right.

07:27.760 --> 07:30.990
I don't mean you're not strong enough.

07:30.990 --> 07:33.720
But could you use your 
magic on another person?

07:34.000 --> 07:36.640
I'm... not sure.

07:36.640 --> 07:38.390
It's one thing if it's an actual fight,

07:38.390 --> 07:41.190
but it's tougher to aim a spell
 at someone than, say, a sword.

07:41.860 --> 07:44.190
If it hits, it could kill them.

07:44.190 --> 07:48.170
Some people are crazy enough 
to never hesitate at all,

07:48.170 --> 07:51.150
but most people couldn't 
just do it immediately.

07:51.670 --> 07:53.570
Is that how it works?

07:55.940 --> 08:01.060
<i>I must be one of the crazy 
people she's talking about.</i>

08:04.920 --> 08:11.980
So as I see it, this Mabel girl is 
probably the choice of some noble.

08:11.980 --> 08:14.800
There you go again with your hatred of nobles.

08:14.800 --> 08:16.720
It's not hatred!

08:16.720 --> 08:21.330
I bet they want to make it so she has 
a tournament appearance on her resume,

08:21.330 --> 08:24.810
to make it easier for her to get a 
high-ranking job in the government.

08:24.810 --> 08:26.150
You really think so?

08:26.150 --> 08:28.370
I'm sure of it!

08:28.370 --> 08:32.120
She'll probably forfeit 
early in the tournament.

08:32.120 --> 08:34.320
She won't want to get hurt.

08:34.320 --> 08:36.490
I'm sure she's never experienced
any real hardship.

08:36.490 --> 08:39.370
You're the one who's never 
experienced hardship.

08:41.620 --> 08:42.490
Mabel.

08:44.680 --> 08:46.880
You're Mabel Crane, then.

08:49.250 --> 08:51.550
So, what are you trying to say?

08:51.550 --> 08:53.960
You babble on, even though you're weak.

08:53.960 --> 08:56.010
And you think that's okay.

08:56.010 --> 08:58.750
You must've been spoiled rotten.

08:59.450 --> 09:03.390
You weren't chosen because 
you were weak. That's all.

09:06.840 --> 09:08.610
Listen to you.

09:11.820 --> 09:13.060
Amyu...

09:13.060 --> 09:15.110
Hey, you two over there.

09:15.550 --> 09:17.320
Give me those practice swords.

09:17.320 --> 09:18.080
Huh?

09:18.800 --> 09:19.980
O-Okay.

09:23.000 --> 09:27.330
You must know how to use a sword,
to be able to talk like that.

09:30.520 --> 09:32.380
What's the point of this?

09:32.380 --> 09:36.580
You're the one who picked the fight. 
Don't make me laugh.

09:42.860 --> 09:44.080
<i>That stance...</i>

09:44.760 --> 09:47.790
<i>She's every bit as practiced as Amyu.</i>

09:48.300 --> 09:50.400
<i>So she can use a sword?</i>

09:50.400 --> 09:54.240
S-Seika, shouldn't we stop them?

09:54.240 --> 09:55.400
It's fine.

09:56.000 --> 09:58.630
Neither of them is that into this.

09:58.630 --> 10:00.030
I'll stop them if I have to.

10:00.800 --> 10:05.000
<i>And it's a good opportunity for me 
to witness Mabel's strength.</i>

10:05.270 --> 10:07.830
Seika, give the signal.

10:07.830 --> 10:09.020
Okay.

10:09.020 --> 10:10.790
Now... begin.

10:15.090 --> 10:15.960
<i>She blocked?</i>

10:27.020 --> 10:28.140
Amyu...

10:45.840 --> 10:48.540
Just keep letting them spoil you.

10:48.800 --> 10:50.960
Pretty little hero.

10:52.710 --> 10:54.500
We weren't supposed to use magic, were we?

10:55.380 --> 10:57.700
At least, I thought we weren't.

10:58.760 --> 11:00.760
<i>So Amyu saw it, too, then.</i>

11:01.460 --> 11:03.930
<i>That's dark magic.</i>

11:04.870 --> 11:06.890
You think you'll get another shot.

11:06.890 --> 11:09.290
That's why you're weak.

11:10.730 --> 11:11.920
And you, too.

11:11.920 --> 11:15.660
If you won't take this seriously, 
you need to forfeit now.

11:15.660 --> 11:17.650
And why's that?

11:17.650 --> 11:21.740
This won't be the kind of tournament 
where nobody gets hurt.

11:21.740 --> 11:24.570
Thanks. I'll think about it.

11:29.710 --> 11:31.850
Amyu, are you hurt?

11:31.850 --> 11:32.940
You okay?

11:37.370 --> 11:39.320
Okay, I've decided.

11:42.870 --> 11:45.100
<i>A while after that,</i>

11:45.100 --> 11:52.310
<i>I found myself in a carriage with 
Mabel heading for the capital.</i>

11:54.840 --> 11:56.820
What are you two doing here?

11:57.500 --> 12:00.070
I'm your servant!

12:00.070 --> 12:02.070
I have to go with you!

12:02.400 --> 12:04.910
Well, you, I get, but...

12:04.910 --> 12:07.270
What, do you have a problem with it?

12:07.270 --> 12:09.330
Did you get permission from the school?

12:11.140 --> 12:12.600
You didn't, did you?

12:13.040 --> 12:14.670
Who cares?

12:15.100 --> 12:21.300
I've never been to the capital and 
I might not get another chance.

12:21.300 --> 12:24.460
<i>She says that, but her real 
goal is to watch the fight.</i>

12:24.460 --> 12:27.440
<i>She's curious to see how Mabel fights.</i>

12:27.440 --> 12:29.690
<i>She's got a stubborn 
streak in her, after all.</i>

12:30.280 --> 12:31.730
Where will you sleep?

12:31.730 --> 12:36.520
In Yifa's room, of course.

12:38.940 --> 12:41.850
Seika, are you okay in the carriage?

12:41.850 --> 12:43.220
No.

12:44.170 --> 12:45.530
Are you carriage-sick?

12:45.870 --> 12:47.020
Pathetic.

12:49.290 --> 12:53.210
You don't show a lot of respect 
for your upperclassmen, do you?

12:53.210 --> 12:55.840
Skill's all that matters in the academy.

12:55.840 --> 12:57.120
That's what I was told.

12:57.120 --> 13:00.170
And I'm the same age as you.

13:00.880 --> 13:02.560
That's rare.

13:02.560 --> 13:05.560
A noble joining the school a year late...

13:05.560 --> 13:08.350
We're all the same age, then.

13:08.350 --> 13:13.730
Um, I started late, too, so I'm 
a year older than all of you.

13:13.730 --> 13:15.690
You did?

13:15.690 --> 13:17.540
Wow, you're older than me?

13:18.910 --> 13:20.560
<i>Well, that explains that.</i>

13:20.560 --> 13:23.030
What are you staring at, Amyu?

13:23.030 --> 13:25.950
I guess they do get bigger 
as you get older, huh?

13:24.720 --> 13:25.950
How annoying.

13:25.950 --> 13:29.120
Aww, don't joke around like that.

13:25.950 --> 13:29.120
Everyone at the academy's like this.

13:29.120 --> 13:30.620
Like what?

13:30.620 --> 13:33.200
I wish you'd share some with me.

13:30.970 --> 13:33.200
Children without a care in the world.

13:33.500 --> 13:36.000
Well, we are kids.

13:36.000 --> 13:37.290
What's wrong with that?

13:37.580 --> 13:39.960
What's wrong is that you 
see nothing wrong with it.

13:40.360 --> 13:41.290
That's...

13:41.720 --> 13:42.630
What?

13:43.000 --> 13:45.020
No, nothing.

13:46.050 --> 13:48.640
<i>I'll keep my mouth shut.</i>

13:48.640 --> 13:51.120
<i>She's right.</i>

13:51.120 --> 13:55.060
Just so we're clear, you're one of them.

13:55.720 --> 13:56.690
Yup.

13:57.790 --> 13:59.440
You may be right.

14:07.450 --> 14:09.210
Look at all the people!

14:09.210 --> 14:12.240
I've never seen such a tall building!

14:12.240 --> 14:15.500
Anyway, is he okay?

14:18.160 --> 14:24.250
Seika, why not head straight for the 
inn instead of the combat grounds?

14:24.250 --> 14:25.800
I'm okay...

14:25.800 --> 14:27.630
<i>I'm not! I'm going to hurl!</i>

14:28.730 --> 14:31.390
I want to see the pairings 
for the tournament.

14:31.600 --> 14:33.510
Huh? Where's Mabel?

14:33.510 --> 14:35.540
You're right... She's not here.

14:35.540 --> 14:37.520
She just disappeared without a word?

14:38.440 --> 14:41.000
Well, let's leave her be for a while.

14:41.000 --> 14:42.970
Seika, are you okay?

14:42.970 --> 14:43.830
Yeah.

14:43.830 --> 14:46.650
We'll have to walk a ways 
to the combat grounds.

14:46.650 --> 14:49.490
This carriage can't travel within the walls.

14:49.490 --> 14:50.990
Want to call a cab?

14:51.670 --> 14:52.940
Are you trying to kill me?

14:54.240 --> 14:56.260
So this is where it's held.

14:56.260 --> 14:57.100
Yup.

14:57.100 --> 14:59.540
But right now, I'm just 
here to look at the board.

14:59.540 --> 15:02.060
Hmm, where's my name?

15:02.930 --> 15:03.710
Here.

15:03.710 --> 15:07.880
<i>So if both Mabel and I win, 
we'll face each other in the semi-finals?</i>

15:08.250 --> 15:12.290
<i>I thought they put deliberate 
thought into the brackets.</i>

15:12.290 --> 15:15.720
<i>But they've got two people from the same 
school fighting in the semi-finals.</i>

15:16.310 --> 15:19.410
Any names you recognize, Amyu?

15:19.410 --> 15:20.540
Nope.

15:20.540 --> 15:24.030
No famous adventurer's going to 
appear in a tournament like this.

15:24.030 --> 15:25.930
I've seen what I wanted to see.

15:25.930 --> 15:27.530
I'm going to get some rest at the inn.

15:27.530 --> 15:29.900
Yeah? I'll go with you, then.

15:29.900 --> 15:31.610
No, it's fine.

15:31.610 --> 15:33.320
I'll just lie down.

15:33.600 --> 15:36.550
Why don't you two explore 
the city until evening?

15:36.550 --> 15:37.550
But...

15:37.950 --> 15:42.560
Yifa, sometimes men want to be alone.

15:42.560 --> 15:44.330
It's a little light out, though.

15:45.120 --> 15:46.710
Y-Yeah?

15:46.970 --> 15:49.170
Hey, don't give her weird ideas.

15:49.170 --> 15:50.450
I'm joking.

15:50.450 --> 15:52.450
He's being nice enough to offer.

15:52.450 --> 15:53.990
Let's go, Yifa.

15:53.990 --> 15:56.810
If Seika and the new girl 
lose in the first round,

15:56.810 --> 15:59.090
we'll have to go home right away.

16:00.400 --> 16:03.190
Okay, Seika. I'll buy something
for you to eat on the way back.

16:03.190 --> 16:05.090
Okay, thanks.

16:05.840 --> 16:12.140
<i>Now then, time to look into why the 
academy chose to send me, not Amyu.</i>

16:17.300 --> 16:19.620
It's time!

16:19.620 --> 16:22.530
The prestigious Capital 
Sword Fighting Tournament,

16:22.530 --> 16:26.250
now the Capital Mixed Disciplines Combat 
Tournament, is about to begin!

16:26.250 --> 16:30.630
The rules have been changed this 
year to allow for the use of magic,

16:31.210 --> 16:36.220
and approximately half of 
the entrants are mages!

16:36.220 --> 16:41.090
A competitor loses if incapacitated,
knocked out of the ring, or they surrender.

16:41.090 --> 16:43.560
The basis for the judges' 
decisions are unchanged,

16:43.560 --> 16:47.310
with one new addition: 
the destruction of your amulet.

16:47.690 --> 16:50.460
<i>They take damage in place of their owner,</i>

16:50.460 --> 16:53.730
<i>and break when too much is absorbed, huh?</i>

16:53.730 --> 16:58.530
<i>The organizers probably intend to use this 
to keep there from being causalities, but...</i>

16:58.530 --> 17:03.210
I'll now introduce our first contestant!

17:03.210 --> 17:06.370
The genius child of the legendary 
Lamprogue clan of mages!

17:06.720 --> 17:08.370
Seika Lamprogue!

17:13.920 --> 17:17.090
We've got our first mage!

17:17.090 --> 17:23.810
His opponent will be the Mad Dog Speedster, 
from the Garlz Mercenary Band,

17:23.810 --> 17:25.450
Dennis Regan!

17:27.690 --> 17:33.320
He's a pure swordsman, and the 
best the Garlz Mercenary Band has!

17:33.320 --> 17:37.880
A former noble who was disowned by 
Viscount Regan for his misbehavior...

17:37.880 --> 17:41.160
Does he still use the family 
name to aggravate his father?

17:41.160 --> 17:42.990
Hey, kid.

17:42.990 --> 17:48.250
I'm a lucky guy, getting to beat the shit 
out of a noble brat in the first round.

17:48.250 --> 17:50.920
Yeah, you don't need to say a word.

17:50.920 --> 17:54.510
I know I'm a shithead, and I don't care.

17:54.510 --> 17:56.380
Mage versus swordsman!

17:56.380 --> 17:59.050
A match-up that represents 
this whole tournament!

17:59.050 --> 18:02.390
What kind of match do they 
have in store for us?

18:02.390 --> 18:05.020
Mages are nice and easy to deal with.

18:05.020 --> 18:07.730
They can't do anything without
someone protecting them.

18:07.730 --> 18:13.320
I can kill a mage 10 times before 
he finishes chanting his dumb spell.

18:13.320 --> 18:17.020
I'm not in good shape today.

18:17.020 --> 18:18.740
My head hurts.

18:18.740 --> 18:22.030
What, are you already making 
excuses for when you lose?

18:22.400 --> 18:26.200
No. I'm saying I'll end this quick.

18:26.200 --> 18:29.170
Match one, round one, begins!

18:29.170 --> 18:31.500
<i>Die</i>!

18:33.600 --> 18:34.710
Bye.

18:35.550 --> 18:36.460
Phase of sun.

18:37.860 --> 18:39.470
Spell of Internal Release.

18:47.420 --> 18:48.710
I-It's over!

18:48.710 --> 18:51.620
The winner is Seika Lamprogue!

18:52.810 --> 18:54.010
Yay!

18:54.010 --> 18:55.880
What did we just witness?

18:55.880 --> 18:59.910
He dodged Dennis's charge 
at a speed too fast to see,

18:59.910 --> 19:02.410
and blew him away in the next instant!

19:02.410 --> 19:04.240
Was that some kind of magic?

19:04.820 --> 19:07.020
<i>He probably won't die from that.</i>

19:07.020 --> 19:08.620
<i>I'll have to be more careful, though.</i>

19:08.620 --> 19:13.130
<i>Well, he wasn't going to hold back, 
either, so I don't really care.</i>

19:16.390 --> 19:19.900
Seika, how many matches do you intend to win?

19:21.060 --> 19:22.390
I'll decide at some point.

19:22.390 --> 19:24.740
It's fine to have some fun,

19:24.740 --> 19:28.470
but I think it's a bad idea 
to stand out too much here.

19:28.750 --> 19:32.330
You've been getting careless lately.

19:32.330 --> 19:34.060
I know, I know.

19:34.060 --> 19:39.660
And aren't you using too many 
shiki at once, even for you?

19:39.660 --> 19:41.240
I'm worried.

19:41.240 --> 19:43.840
No, it's needed.

19:44.490 --> 19:47.040
It's more important than 
the tournament, actually.

19:52.160 --> 19:54.040
Okay, all clear.

19:56.420 --> 19:57.460
Seika!

19:57.820 --> 19:59.890
Congratulations on your first win!

19:59.890 --> 20:02.380
Yeah, thanks for cheering me on.

20:02.380 --> 20:04.550
Okay, let's welcome our next entrant!

20:04.970 --> 20:08.110
Belem, the finest student of Sage Ford.

20:08.110 --> 20:13.140
Sage Ford is famous for his many 
successes as a water mage...

20:13.140 --> 20:17.230
What kind of magic will
Belem show us today?

20:17.760 --> 20:23.530
His opponent is Kyle, a guard from 
the Rugrock Merchants Association!

20:23.530 --> 20:26.560
We have very little information about him!

20:26.560 --> 20:30.250
From his strange appearance, it's hard to even
say if he's either a mage or a swordsman...

20:30.250 --> 20:32.120
What techniques will he use?

20:32.400 --> 20:34.000
Let's find out!

20:34.310 --> 20:36.170
Let the match begin!

20:36.170 --> 20:37.540
Here I go!

20:41.390 --> 20:42.220
<i>What?</i>

20:42.920 --> 20:44.240
What just happened?

20:44.240 --> 20:47.100
Belem's not moving at all.

20:47.360 --> 20:50.560
Kyle is slowly approaching.

20:51.820 --> 20:53.890
<i>His face is twisted with fear.</i>

21:11.610 --> 21:13.470
Belem has been incapacitated!

21:13.470 --> 21:15.370
The winner is Kyle!

21:15.370 --> 21:18.130
We have our first fatality of the tournament!

21:18.130 --> 21:20.300
But what did we just see?

21:20.300 --> 21:24.720
I'm curious why Kyle didn't make 
any attempt to stop his sword...

21:24.720 --> 21:28.340
But what strange event
did we all just witness?

21:29.800 --> 21:31.680
You're kidding me...

21:32.100 --> 21:33.740
<i>They're all so excited.</i>

21:33.740 --> 21:37.650
<i>I guess even in this world, 
people like watching others die.</i>

21:38.770 --> 21:40.800
<i>His expression hasn't changed.</i>

21:40.800 --> 21:42.550
<i>He's a veteran killer.</i>

21:43.130 --> 21:45.860
<i>They said he was a Rugrock
Merchants Association guard,</i>

21:46.310 --> 21:47.840
<i>but that's almost certainly a lie.</i>

21:47.840 --> 21:51.080
<i>He's probably someone with a dark 
history, sent from who-knows-where.</i>

21:51.080 --> 21:54.660
His opponent couldn't move a muscle.

21:55.540 --> 21:57.480
<i>I guess they exist in this world, too...</i>

21:57.480 --> 22:02.090
<i>Casters who put spiritual power into 
their gaze and curse hose they look...</i>

22:02.550 --> 22:03.930
<i>Bearers of the Evil Eye.</i>
